theory.intro:
When $\theta>0$, a negative angle $-\theta$ is a clockwise rotation through $\theta$ from the positive $x$-axis. On the unit circle, replacing $\theta$ with $-\theta$ reflects $P(x,y)$ across the $x$-axis to $P'(x,-y)$, establishing the identities $\cos(-\theta)=\cos\theta$, $\sin(-\theta)=-\sin\theta$, and $\tan(-\theta)=-\tan\theta$ where tangent is defined.

